{"id":"mahabharata-3-142","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":142,"title":"द्विचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 142 · Yudhishthira's resolve to see Arjuna","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira tells his brothers and Draupadi that all beings meet their fate, that the wicked Kauravas will fall, and that Arjuna, generous and mighty, will rejoin them. Living on little food, they will climb Mount Gandhamadana to meet him.","kn":"ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳೂ ವಿಧಿಯನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ, ದುಷ್ಟ ಕೌರವರು ಬೀಳುವರು, ಉದಾರ ಬಲಿಷ್ಠ ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಸೇರುವನು ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಸಹೋದರರಿಗೂ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಗೂ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮಿತಾಹಾರಿಗಳಾಗಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕಾಣಲು ಗಂಧಮಾದನ ಪರ್ವತವೇರೋಣ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर भाइयों और द्रौपदी से कहते हैं कि सब प्राणी अपने भाग्य से मिलते हैं, दुष्ट कौरव गिरेंगे और उदार तथा पराक्रमी अर्जुन उनसे फिर मिलेंगे। अल्प भोजन पर रहते हुए वे उनसे मिलने गन्धमादन पर्वत पर चढ़ेंगे।","te":"అన్ని జీవులూ విధిని ఎదుర్కొంటాయని, దుష్ట కౌరవులు పతనమవుతారని, ఉదారుడు బలవంతుడైన అర్జునుడు మళ్లీ కలుస్తాడని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు సోదరులకు, ద్రౌపదికి చెబుతాడు. మితాహారులై అతనిని కలవడానికి గంధమాదన పర్వతం ఎక్కుదామంటాడు.","ta":"எல்லா உயிர்களும் விதியைச் சந்திக்கும், தீய கௌரவர்கள் வீழ்வர், தாராளமும் வலிமையுமுள்ள அர்ஜுனன் மீண்டும் சேர்வான் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் சகோதரர்களிடமும் திரௌபதியிடமும் சொல்கிறார். குறைந்த உணவுடன் அவனைக் காண கந்தமாதன மலையில் ஏறுவோம் என்கிறார்.","ml":"എല്ലാ ജീവികളും അവരവരുടെ വിധി അനുഭവിക്കുമെന്നും ദുഷ്ടന്മാരായ കൗരവർ വീഴുമെന്നും, ഉദാരനും ശക്തനുമായ അർജുനൻ തങ്ങളോട് വീണ്ടും ചേരുമെന്നും യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ സഹോദരന്മാരോടും ദ്രൗപദിയോടും പറയുന്നു. ചെറിയ ആഹാരം കഴിച്ച്, അർജുനനെ കാണാൻ അവർ ഗന്ധമാദനപർവതം കയറുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.142; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भीमसेन यमौ चोभौ पाञ्चालि च निबोधत ।\nनास्ति भूतस्य नाशो वै पश्यतास्मान्वनेचरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, you twins, and Panchali, listen. A being never perishes, though you see us as forest-dwellers."}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्बलाः क्लेशिताः स्मेति यद्ब्रवीथेतरेतरम् ।\nअशक्येऽपि व्रजामेति धनंजयदिदृक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"You say to each other that we are weak and weary, and that we go on though it may be impossible, wanting to see Dhananjaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"तन्मे दहति गात्राणि तूलराशिमिवानलः ।\nयच्च वीरं न पश्यामि धनंजयमुपान्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"It burns my limbs like fire on a heap of cotton, that I do not see the hero Dhananjaya near me."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्य दर्शनतृष्णं मां सानुजं वनमास्थितम् ।\nयाज्ञसेन्याः परामर्शः स च वीर दहत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am in the forest with my brothers, thirsting for the sight of him, and that touching of Draupadi by the enemy also burns me, hero."}},{"n":5,"text":"नकुलात्पूर्वजं पार्थं न पश्याम्यमितौजसम् ।\nअजेयमुग्रधन्वानं तेन तप्ये वृकोदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrikodara, I do not see Partha, elder to Nakula, of boundless might, unconquerable, with his terrible bow, and that is why I burn."}},{"n":6,"text":"तीर्थानि चैव रम्याणि वनानि च सरांसि च ।\nचरामि सह युष्माभिस्तस्य दर्शनकाङ्क्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wander with you to holy places, lovely forests and lakes, wanting to see him."}},{"n":7,"text":"पञ्च वर्षाण्यहं वीरं सत्यसंधं धनंजयम् ।\nयन्न पश्यामि बीभत्सुं तेन तप्ये वृकोदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"For five years I have not seen that hero, the true-to-his-word Dhananjaya, Bibhatsu, and that is why I burn, Vrikodara."}},{"n":8,"text":"तं वै श्यामं गुडाकेशं सिंहविक्रान्तगामिनम् ।\nन पश्यामि महाबाहुं तेन तप्ये वृकोदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not see him, dark-skinned, with thick locks, who walks with a lion's stride, the mighty-armed. That is why I burn, Vrikodara."}},{"n":9,"text":"कृतास्त्रं निपुणं युद्धे प्रतिमानं धनुष्मताम् ।\nन पश्यामि नरश्रेष्ठं तेन तप्ये वृकोदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not see that best of men, skilled in weapons, expert in battle, the model of all archers, and so I burn."}},{"n":10,"text":"चरन्तमरिसंघेषु कालं क्रुद्धमिवान्तकम् ।\nप्रभिन्नमिव मातङ्गं सिंहस्कन्धं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya moves among the hosts of enemies like Death in anger, like a rutting elephant, with the shoulders of a lion."}},{"n":11,"text":"यः स शक्रादनवरो वीर्येण द्रविणेन च ।\nयमयोः पूर्वजः पार्थः श्वेताश्वोऽमितविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who is no less than Indra in valour and wealth, the elder of the twins, Partha with the white horses, of boundless prowess,"}},{"n":12,"text":"दुःखेन महताविष्टः स्वकृतेनानिवर्तिना ।\nअजेयमुग्रधन्वानं तं न पश्यामि फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am overwhelmed by great sorrow, brought by my own deeds, and I cannot turn it back. I do not see that Phalguna, unconquerable, with his terrible bow."}},{"n":13,"text":"सततं यः क्षमाशीलः क्षिप्यमाणोऽप्यणीयसा ।\nऋजुमार्गप्रपन्नस्य शर्मदाताभयस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is always forbearing even when slighted by the smallest man. To one who has taken an honest path he gives happiness and safety."}},{"n":14,"text":"स तु जिह्मप्रवृत्तस्य माययाभिजिघांसतः ।\nअपि वज्रधरस्यापि भवेत्कालविषोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But against the one who acts crookedly and tries to kill him by trickery, he becomes like deadly poison, even if that man wields the thunderbolt."}},{"n":15,"text":"शत्रोरपि प्रपन्नस्य सोऽनृशंसः प्रतापवान् ।\nदाताभयस्य बीभत्सुरमितात्मा महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even to an enemy who takes refuge he is gentle and mighty. Bibhatsu, of boundless spirit and great strength, gives safety."}},{"n":16,"text":"सर्वेषामाश्रयोऽस्माकं रणेऽरीणां प्रमर्दिता ।\nआहर्ता सर्वरत्नानां सर्वेषां नः सुखावहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the refuge of us all, the crusher of foes in battle, the bringer of all jewels, and a bringer of happiness to all of us."}},{"n":17,"text":"रत्नानि यस्य वीर्येण दिव्यान्यासन्पुरा मम ।\nबहूनि बहुजातानि यानि प्राप्तः सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By his valour I once had many divine jewels, which Suyodhana later got."}},{"n":18,"text":"यस्य बाहुबलाद्वीर सभा चासीत्पुरा मम ।\nसर्वरत्नमयी ख्याता त्रिषु लोकेषु पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, by the strength of his arm my assembly hall once existed, famed in the three worlds as made wholly of jewels, Pandava."}},{"n":19,"text":"वासुदेवसमं वीर्ये कार्तवीर्यसमं युधि ।\nअजेयमजितं युद्धे तं न पश्यामि फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Equal to Vasudeva in valour, equal to Kartavirya in battle, unconquerable and unconquered in battle, I do not see that Phalguna."}},{"n":20,"text":"संकर्षणं महावीर्यं त्वां च भीमापराजितम् ।\nअनुजातः स वीर्येण वासुदेवं च शत्रुहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Sankarshana, and you, Bhima, undefeated, and Vasudeva: Arjuna, the slayer of foes, is equal to them in valour."}},{"n":21,"text":"यस्य बाहुबले तुल्यः प्रभावे च पुरंदरः ।\nजवे वायुर्मुखे सोमः क्रोधे मृत्युः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In strength of arm he equals Indra in power, Vayu in speed, Soma in his face, and eternal Death in anger."}},{"n":22,"text":"ते वयं तं नरव्याघ्रं सर्वे वीर दिदृक्षवः ।\nप्रवेक्ष्यामो महाबाहो पर्वतं गन्धमादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So all of us, hero, wishing to see that tiger among men, shall enter the mountain Gandhamadana, mighty-armed."}},{"n":23,"text":"विशाला बदरी यत्र नरनारायणाश्रमः ।\nतं सदाध्युषितं यक्षैर्द्रक्ष्यामो गिरिमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We shall see that best of mountains, always inhabited by yakshas, where the great Badari tree stands, the hermitage of Nara and Narayana."}},{"n":24,"text":"कुबेरनलिनीं रम्यां राक्षसैरभिरक्षिताम् ।\nपद्भिरेव गमिष्यामस्तप्यमाना महत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We shall go on foot, practising great austerity, to Kubera's lovely lotus lake, guarded by rakshasas."}},{"n":25,"text":"नातप्ततपसा शक्यो देशो गन्तुं वृकोदर ।\nन नृशंसेन लुब्धेन नाप्रशान्तेन भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrikodara, that region cannot be reached by one who has not practised austerity, nor by the cruel, the greedy, or the restless."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत्र सर्वे गमिष्यामो भीमार्जुनपदैषिणः ।\nसायुधा बद्धनिस्त्रिंशाः सह विप्रैर्महाव्रतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We shall all go there, seeking the footsteps of Bhima and Arjuna, armed and with swords girded, along with brahmins of great vows."}},{"n":27,"text":"मक्षिकान्मशकान्दंशान्व्याघ्रान्सिंहान्सरीसृपान् ।\nप्राप्नोत्यनियतः पार्थ नियतस्तान्न पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, an undisciplined man meets flies, mosquitoes, gadflies, tigers, lions and snakes, but the disciplined does not see them."}},{"n":28,"text":"ते वयं नियतात्मानः पर्वतं गन्धमादनम् ।\nप्रवेक्ष्यामो मिताहारा धनंजयदिदृक्षवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, with our minds restrained, eating little, wishing to see Dhananjaya, we shall enter the mountain Gandhamadana."}}]}]}